    dict(key='10-act-4', kind='console', title='Act Four — Counting out, by a recursive formula',
         body='FOUR. Counting out, by a recursive formula.\n  J(1) = 0, J(n) = (J(n - 1) + k) mod n: winner at position 3 of 5 with k = 3, depth 5\n  position 3 is Dan: the same winner the list simulation finds, without the list\n  41 players, k = 3: winner at position 30, depth 41',
         narration='The counting-out game has a recursive formula. [[slnc 400]] With one player, the winner is at position zero. [[slnc 400]] With n players, the winner is the winner for n minus one, moved on k places, round the circle. [[slnc 500]] For five players, counting in threes, the formula says position three: Dan. [[slnc 400]] The same winner, without building the circle.'),
